Create a lesson plan that integrates drama, mime or theater techniques into a history class. Duration: 3 class periods (each lasts for 45 minutes) for 3 days
Topic: Opium Wars between China and Britain
Grade level: 9-10
[The Start of Assistant 1’s Answer]
Day 1
Warm-up (5 min): Have students imagine they are a piece of furniture in the room. They must move around the room without making any noise.

Introduction (5 min): Teacher will introduce the background of the Opium Wars and the conflicts between China and Britain.

Drama exercise (30 min): Students will be divided into two groups. One group will act as the British and the other group will act as the Chinese. The British group will act out the following dialogue:
British: “We have something very valuable to trade with you.”
Chinese: “We don’t need anything from you.”
British: “But we have something you want.”
Chinese: “We don’t need anything from you. Please leave.”
British: “If you don’t accept our trade, we will use force.”
Chinese: “You can’t force us.”
British: “We will use our military power to take over your country.”

The Chinese group will act out the following dialogue:
Chinese: “We don’t want to fight with you. Please leave peacefully.”
British: “We don’t want to fight either, but we have no choice.”
Chinese: “If you attack us, we will fight back.”
British: “You will lose.”
Chinese: “We will fight to the death.”

Day 2
Warm-up (5 min): Have students imagine they are an animal in the zoo. They must move around the classroom and make the sounds of the animal.

Introduction (5 min): Teacher will go over the drama exercise from yesterday and discuss the conflicts between China and Britain.

